{
  "id": "Compound::DB00855 - Gene::6564",
  "verbalization": "Aminolevulinic Acid appears to interact with Slc15a1 through a shared pathway involving Slc15a2, which participates in multiple transport activities. These include proton-dependent peptide transport, peptide/proton cotransport, and proton/oligonucleotide cotransport. The evidence suggests that Aminolevulinic Acid binds to Slc15a2, which in turn participates in transport processes that ultimately involve Slc15a1. This implies a potential functional link between Aminolevulinic Acid and Slc15a1, possibly through the modulation of Slc15a2's transport activity. The consistent binding of Aminolevulinic Acid to Slc15a2 and its participation in transport processes that engage Slc15a1 suggests a mechanism by which Aminolevulinic Acid may influence Slc15a1's function, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be elucidated.",
